ral calamities and/or acts of violence.\n\nForward-looking statements reflect the current views of our Company as of the period of these results and are not a guarantee of future\nperformance. These statements are based on our management\u2019s beliefs, assumptions, current plans, estimates and expectations, which in turn are\nbased on currently available information. Although we believe the assumptions upon which these forward-looking statements are based are\nreasonable, any of these assumptions could prove to be inaccurate, and the forward-looking statements based on these assumptions could be\nincorrect. We undertake no obligation to update forward-looking statements to reflect events or circumstances after the date there.\n\nThe Company disclaims any obligation or liability to any person for any loss or damage caused by errors or omissions, whether arising from\nnegligence or any other cause. Recipients of this presentation are not to construe its contents, or any prior or subsequent communications from or\nwith the Company or its representatives as investment, legal or tax advice. In addition, this presentation does not purport to be complete or\ncontain all information that may be required to make a full analysis of the Company. These materials do not constitute or form part of any offer or\nsolicitation to purchase or subscribe for securities of the Company.\n\n---\n\n## OUR PURPOSE\n\n\"To give every Indian the\nconfidence to access\nthe best healthcare\n\n---\n\n**Executive Summary Q3\u2019FY25 | 9M\u2019FY25**\n\n(\u20b9 in Crores)\n\n| Category | Q3'FY25 (\u20b9 in Crores) | 9M'FY25 (\u20b9 in Crores) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GWP (Without 1/n) | 1769.8 | 5011.3 |\n| GWP (With 1/n) | 1442.1 | 4683.6 |\n| Profit/(Loss) After Tax (I-GAAP) | 13.2 | 7.4 |\n| Profit/(Loss) After Tax (IFRS) | 60.0 | 119.5 |\n| Combined Ratio (Without 1/n) | 96.3 | 100.9 |\n| Combined Ratio (With 1/n) | 108.3 | 105.0 |\n| Claims Settlement Ratio | 91.8 | 92.1 |\n| Weighted Episodal NPS | 56 | 53 |\n\n<sup>1</sup>Profit after Tax (I-GAAP) increased from Rs. -75.2 crore in 9M\u2019FY24 to Rs 7.4 crore in 9M\u2019FY25\n\n<sup>2</sup>Positive change in Combined Ratio reflects improvement over previous year\n\n**YoY Change**\n\nW.e.f. October 1, 2024 Long-term products are accounted on 1/n, as mandated by IRDAI, hence Q3 & 9M\u2019FY2025 numbers are not comparable\n\n---\n\n## Agenda\n\nOur Strategy\n\nFinancial Performance\n\n---\n\n**1**\n\n**Building a** \n**Granular, Growth** \n**Oriented and** \n**Profitable Health** \n**Insurance** \n**Franchise**\n\n**2**\n\n**Health Partner of** \n**Choice for** \n**Customers**\n\n**3**\n\n**Multi-Channel &** \n**Diversified** \n**Distribution with** \n**Emphasis on** \n**Digital Sales**\n\n**4**\n\n**Technology &** \n**Analytics Driven** \n**Business Model**\n\n**5**\n\n**Disciplined** \n**Underwriting &** \n**Claims** \n**Management,** \n**Underpinned by** \n**Expertise**\n\n**6**\n\n**Focus on Talent** \n**Management &** \n**Execution**\n\n---\n\n## Key Performance Indicators (1/3)\n\n| Particulars | Unit | FY2023 | FY2024 | 9M'FY2024 | 9M'FY2025 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Gross Written Premium1 (GWP) | (\u20b9 in Crores) | 4,073.0 | 5,607.6 | 3,848.1 | 4,683.6 |\n| Net Written Premium | (\u20b9 in Crores) | 3,183.1 | 4,421.0 | 3,039.0 | 3,697.3 |\n| Net Earned Premium | (\u20b9 in Crores) | 2,662.8 | 3,811.2 | 2,593.2 | 3,367.0 |\n| Profit/(Loss) After Tax (I-GAAP) | (\u20b9 in Crores) | 12.5 | 81.9 | -75.2 | 7.4 |\n| Profit/(Loss) After Tax (IFRS) | (\u20b9 in Crores) | 8.5 | 106.4 | 45.1 | 119.5 |\n| Combined Ratio | % | 97.2% | 98.8% | 103.2% | 105.0% |\n| Claims Ratio | % | 54.1% | 59.0% | 63.1% | 63.4% |\n| Expense Ratio | % | 43.2% | 39.8% | 40.1% | 41.6% |\n| Expense of Management as % of GWP | % | 41.2% | 39.3% | 39.5% | 39.0% |\n| Retention Ratio (NWP/GWP) | % | 78.2% | 78.8% | 79.0% | 78.9% |\n| Net Worth | (\u20b9 in Crores) | 831.1 | 2,049.6 | 1,891.3 | 2,868.9 |\n| Return on Average Net Worth2 | % | 1.9% | 5.7% | -5.5% | 0.3% |\n| Solvency Ratio | Times | 1.67x | 2.55x | 2.56x | 3.03x |\n| Assets Under Management | (\u20b9 in Crores) | 3,366.1 | 5,458.2 | 5,231.2 | 7,310.7 |\n| Yield on Total Investments (Annualized) | % | 6.7% | 7.1% | 7.1% | 7.4% |\n\nW.e.f. October 1, 2024 Long-term products are accounted on 1/n, as mandated by IRDAI, hence 9M\u2019FY2025 numbers are not comparable\n<sup>1</sup>No Reinsurance Accepted, so \u201cGWP = GDPI\u201d  <sup>2</sup>Return on Average Net Worth is not annualized for 9M\u2019FY2024 & 9M\u2019FY2025\n\n---\n\n## Key Performance Indicators (2/3)\n\n| Particulars | Unit | FY2023 | FY2024 | 9M'FY2024 | 9M'FY2025 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Retail Health GWP | (\u20b9 in Crores) | 2,969.7 | 3,839.7 | 2,585.1 | 3,136.0 |\n| Retail Health Market Share | % | 8.4% | 9.1% | 9.0% | 9.6% |\n| Retail Health Accretion Market Share | % | 17.3% | 12.9% | 11.8% | 13.4% |\n| Number of Active Lives Insured at the end of the Fiscal | (# in Millions) | 9.9 | 14.7 | 12.6 | 19.8 |\n| Network Hospitals | # | 10,005 | 10,460 | 10,299 | 10,299 |\n| % of Cashless Claims through Network Hospitals | % | 66.5% | 70.0% | 68.1% | 72.6% |\n| Claim Settlement Ratio | % | 90.5% | 91.9% | 91.6% | 92.1% |\n| GWP Contribution of New Retail Health Indemnity Policies with Sum Insured >= \u20b9 1 million | % | 67.4% | 70.7% | 69.9% | 74.1% |\n| Renewal Rate for Retail Health Indemnity Products (by value)3 | % | 89.4% | 92.2% | 93.2% | 87.8% |\n| Avg. Ticket size per policy | \u20b9 | 26,084 | 28,797 | 30,014 | 29,873 |\n| GWP per policy sold by Agents | \u20b9 | 22,895 | 25,028 | 24,324 | 23,790 |\n\nW.e.f. October 1, 2024 Long-term products are accounted on 1/n, as mandated by IRDAI, hence 9M\u2019FY2025 numbers are not comparable\n<sup>3</sup>Renewal rate is calculated on total premium realized from the policies which are renewed in the relevant fiscal period\n\n---\n\n## Key Performance Indicators - Without 1/n (3/3)\n\n| Particulars | Unit | FY2023 | FY2024 | 9M'FY2024 | 9M'FY2025 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Gross Written Premium1 (GWP) | (\u20b9 in Crores) | 4,073.0 | 5,607.6 | 3,848.1 | 5,011.3 |\n| Combined Ratio | % | 97.2% | 98.8% | 103.2% | 100.9% |\n| Claims Ratio | % | 54.1% | 59.0% | 63.1% | 61.1% |\n| Expense Ratio | % | 43.2% | 39.8% | 40.1% | 39.8% |\n| Retail Health GWP | (\u20b9 in Crores) | 2,969.7 | 3,839.7 | 2,585.1 | 3,319.3 |\n| Retail Health GWP Growth | % | 37.7% | 29.3% | 26.1% | 28.4% |\n| Avg. Ticket size per policy | \u20b9 | 26,084 | 28,797 | 30,014 | 31,963 |\n| GWP per policy sold by Agents | \u20b9 | 22,895 | 25,028 | 24,324 | 25,097 |\n| GWP contribution of new retail health indemnity policies with sum insured >= \u20b9 1 million | % | 67.4% | 70.7% | 69.9% | 75.1% |\n\n---\n\n## 1 Building a Granular, Growth Oriented and Profitable Health Insurance Franchise\n\n**Product Mix**\n\n(By GWP)\n\n**Retail Health GWP & Market Share**\n\n(\u20b9 in Crores)\n\n| Category | Retail Health (By GWP, %) | Group Health (By GWP, %) | PA & Travel (By GWP, %) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| FY2023 | 72.9 | 25.0 | 2.1 |\n| FY2024 | 68.5 | 29.5 | 2.0 |\n| 9M'FY2024 | 67.2 | 30.9 | 2.0 |\n| 9M'FY2025 | 67.0 | 30.8 | 2.3 |\n\n| Category | Retail Health GWP (\u20b9 in Crores) | Retail Health Market Share (%) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| FY2023 | 2969.7 | 8.4 |\n| FY2024 | 3839.7 | 9.1 |\n| 9M'FY2024 | 2585.1 | 9.0 |\n| 9M'FY2025 | 3136.0 | 9.6 |\n\n---\n\n## Comprehensive Portfolio of Innovative Health Insurance Products Across All Stages 2 of the Customer Lifecyle\n\n**WELLNESS FOCUSED**\n\n**DISEASE**\n**MANAGEMENT**\n\nReAssure GoActive\nReAssure 2.0\n\n**DISEASE MANAGEMENT**\nsmart HEALTH\n\nHEALTH\n\nAGE\n\nniva Health Insurance\n\nSALES PROCESS\n\nINCOME\n\n**EMBEDDED**\nsmart HEALTH\n\n**ADVISORY**\nTravel Assure\n**HEALTH PLUS**\n\nAspire elixir\n\nSENIOR FIRST\n\n**MASS MARKET**\n**TIERED NETWORK RIDER**\n\n**MASS AFFLUENT**\n**HEALTH PULSE**\n\n**AFFLUENT**\nReAssure ReAssure 2.0\n\n**HNI** PREMIA\n\nXpress Health\n\n**HEALTH PLUS**\n\n**All Retail Products**\n\n**MILLENNIALS**\n\n**Product with \u201cIndustry-First\u201d Features**\n\n**SENIOR CITIZEN**\n\n---\n\n## Enabling Access to a 360\u00b0 Health and Wellness Ecosystem Platform, Providing a 2 Holistic Customer Health Proposition\n\n## HEALTH OFFERINGS\n\n+\n\nHome delivery of medicines\n\n\u68c0\u67e5\n\nBooking individual diagnostic \ntests with home sample \ncollection\n\nTeaching\n\nDigital consultations and \nsecond medical opinion\n\n+\n\nAccess health education \ncontent on diseases published \nby Bupa and wellness content\n\nApp Downloads\n7.2 Million+ \n[Image: Image439]\n[Image: Image435]\n\nLTE 1:23 niva Health Insurance ABC Our Health & Wellness Offerings Health Check-up Doctor Consultation 2nd Medical Opinion Physiotherapy at Home Disease A-Z Health Assessment Niva Bupa Advantage Hassle free claims Cashless claim processing 10,000+ Pan-India cashless network of hospitals 24 X 7 Insta Assist 24X7 customer self-service tool ensuring instant resolution for your service needs. Home My Policy Claims More Monthly Active Users\n\nMonthly Active Users \n4.4 Lakh \n[Image: Image437]\n\n| Category | Steps |\n| --- | --- |\n| 3 May | 9000 |\n| 4 May | 12400 |\n| 5 May | 6500 |\n| 6 May | 300 |\n| 7 May | 100 |\n\nMonthly Average\nHealth Checkups - 30K+\nDoctor Consultation - 6K+\n[Image: Image435] [Image: Image441]\n\n## WELLNESS OFFERINGS\n\nActivity tracker\n\nS\n\nCurated products offering \ndiscounts if a minimum step \ncount is achieved to \nencourage healthy living\n\nHealth assessment tools such as \nBMI and stress calculator\n\nHealthcare provider quality \nand infrastructure matrix\n\nAndroid Rating - 4.5\niOS Rating - 4.7\n[Image: Image443]\n[Image: Image435]\n\n---\n\n## We Measure NPS Across 35 Touch Points and are Focused on Continuously 2 Improving Customer Experience\n\n**Weighted Episodal NPS**\n\n| Category | Weighted Episodal NPS |\n| --- | --- |\n| FY2023 | 38 |\n| FY2024 | 50 |\n| 9M'FY2025 | 53 |\n\n| Category | Claims Cashless Discharge NPS |\n| --- | --- |\n| FY2023 | 62 |\n| FY2024 | 63 |\n| 9M'FY2025 | 66 |\n\n\u2022 Weighted Episodal NPS for 9M\u2019FY2025 stands at +53 which is +3 points higher than FY2024\n\n\u2022 25 Lakh+ customers were reached out seeking feedback in 9M\u2019FY2025\n\n\u2022 2 Lakh+ customer responses received in 9M\u2019FY2025\n\n**Note:**\n1. NPS score of few critical touch points (claims discharge, service, policy issuance, renewal etc.) is combined into a single, weighted NPS score, \ncalculated as weighted average by response method, for the organisation\n\n---\n\n## 3 Multi-Channel & Diversified Distribution with Emphasis on Digital Sales\n\n<u><strong>Diversified Channel Mix with Strong Focus on Growing High Value Channels</strong></u>\n9M\u2019FY2025 (%)\n\nIndividual Agents\n\nCorporate Agent -\nBanks\n\nCorporate Agent -\nOthers\n\n**Diversified Channel Mix with Strong Focus on Growing High Value Channels**\n\n| Category | Share of channel mix, 9M FY2025 (%) |\n| --- | --- |\n| Individual Agents | 29.7 |\n| Corporate Agent - Banks | 20.3 |\n| Corporate Agent - Others | 8.2 |\n| Brokers(1) | 29.0 |\n| Direct Business | 12.2 |\n| Others(2) | 0.6 |\n\n**Notes:**\n\n<u><strong>Pan-India Presence</strong></u>\n\n**212** Branches\n(+1 in Q3\u2019FY25)\n[Image: Image456]\n[Image: Image454]\n\n**172,505** Individual \nAgents\n(+9K in Q3\u2019FY25)\n[Image: Image458]\n[Image: Image454]\n\n**97** Banca & \nOther Corporate \nAgency Partners\n(+11 in Q3\u2019FY25)\n[Image: Image454] [Image: Image460]\n\n1. Brokers include PB Fintech (Policybazaar)\n\n2. Others include Web Aggregators,, Insurance Marketing Firms, Point of Sales and Common Service Centers\n\n**516** Brokers (+8 in Q3'FY25)\n\nMetrics as of 9M\u2019FY2025\n\n## Banks and Other Corporate Agents\n\nHDFC BANK We understand your world\n\nIDFC FIRST Bank\nALWAYS YOU FIRST\n\n## +88 more Corporate Agents\n\n## Insurance Brokers\n\npolicybazaar com\nHAR FAMILY HOGI INSURED\n\n## PhonePe\n\nmahindra INSURANCE BROKERS\n\nturtlemint\n**+511 Others**\n\n+511 Others Notes:\n\n---\n\n## 4 Our Technology Enables us to Serve Customers Anywhere, Anytime\n\n**Digital Self-Serve Capabilities**\n\n**Insta Assist and** \n**Cia Chatbot**\n\n**Cia Chatbot**\n\nniva LTE 1:23 Support\n\nInsta Assist\nReal Time Assistance For Niva Bupa Customers\n\nSearch query by keywords (eg. Claim Status, Policy\n\nClaim Status Renew Policy\n\nSubmit Additional Claim Documents\n\nCia - Health Insurance Partner\nYour Digital Service Assistant\n\nyou today.\n\nPlease select from the given options below:\n\nMon 3:13 PM\n\nService Assistance\n\nMon 3:13 PM\n\nSure , select the option you'd like to know more about:\n\nMon 3:13 PM\n\nClaim Status Application Status\n\nPolicy Documents Hospital Network\n\nKnow Claim Procedure\n\n## Claim Submission\n\n## Claim Submission Cia Chatbot\n\nniva\n12:23\nSubmit Claim\n\nPLEASE SUBMIT AND VERIFY YOUR POLICY DETAILS\nNon-Corporate policy\nCorporate policy\nSelect Option\nPolicy Number\n:\nDate of Birth\n\nSUBMIT\n\n*Please ensure that you are ready with the scanned copy of the claim documents as per claim submission check list.\n\n## One-Click Renewal\n\nniva\nRenew policy\nHi, **ABC**\nHere are the details of your renewal policy\nPlan Name\nReAssure\nPolicy Number\nPolicy Expiry\n10/04/2024\nMember Name\nCurrent Sum\nInsured\nPayable Premium\n25 Lacs\n\u20b9 39,346\n1 Year Premium\n\u20b9 39,346\nPAY NOW\n\n**99.9%** new policies applied \nvia website and mobile apps\n[Image: Image497]\n[Image: Image495]\n\n**90.8%** renewals \ncompleted without human \nintervention\n[Image: Image501]\n[Image: Image499]\n\n**89.5%** cashless claims \nprocessed in <**30 mins**\n[Image: Image505]\n[Image: Image503]\n\n**91.0%** claims submitted \ndigitally\n[Image: Image507]\n[Image: Image503]\n\n---\n\n## Our Value Chain is Significantly Automated with Analytics Embedded into 4 Operations\n\n**Partner Onboarding**\n\nModular API based\npartner integration\n\n**Customer Sourcing**\n\nDigital Dukaan and Niva Bupa \nUNO mobile applications for \nagent training\n\n**99.9%**\n\nNew policies applied \ndigitally\n\n**Underwriting**\n\nRule based automated \ndecisioning\n\nPayments made digitally\n\nReal-time lead scoring \nsupported by product \nrecommendation engine\n\n**Claims Management**\n\nRetail policies autodecisioned\n\n**91.0%**\n\nDigital claims submission\n\nLTV-based approach to \nidentify upsell or cross-sell \nopportunities\n\nReal-time fraud \ndetection capability\n\nOutlier detection tool used \nfor billing review\n\n**28.6%**\n\nCashless Claims Auto-\nAdjudication\n\n**Policy Renewal**\n\nPolicy renewal without \nhuman intervention\n\nPredictive machine-based \nlearning model to target \nhigh lapse probability cases\n\n---\n\n## 5 Disciplined Underwriting and Business Selection Through LTV-Based Approach\n\n## Product-to-customer, segment- PROFILE EXPERIENCE\n\n**COST OF** \n**ACQUISITION**\n\nCUSTOMER CLAIMS \nPROFILE EXPERIENCE\nLOCATION\nRISK PERCEPTION\nRETURN ON\n\n**MEDICAL** \n**INFLATION**\n\n**FUTURE**\n**PREMIUM**\n**CHANGE**\n\n**INVESTMENT**\n**INCOME**\n\n**REQUIRED**\n**CAPITAL**\n\n**DISTRIBUTION**\n**CHANNEL**\n\n**LTV-**\n**Based** \n**Scale**\n\n**COHORT-WISE** \n**LOSS RATIO**\n\n**Rating**\n\n**Follow-Up** \n**Action**\n\n## Action RISK PERCEPTION\nSignificant Over Index LTV-\n\n<u>Significant</u>\nVery High\nHigh\nAcceptable\nNegative\n\n**Product-to-customer, segmentto-channel mapping**\n[Image: Image633]\n\n## Decision Vectors\n\n**Identify opportunities** for upsell \nor cross-sell to customers with \nhigh LTV\n[Image: Image633]\n\n**Customized** and pre-qualified \noffers for each customer\n[Image: Image633]\n\n**Sales channel alignment** of\n\nincentives and monthly review \nto increase renewals\n[Image: Image633]\n\nUse **differentiated interventions**\n\nto maximize customer retention\n[Image: Image633]\n\n---\n\n## 5 Our Multi-Pronged Claims Management Strategy\n\n1 **Developing Partnerships and Strengthening Relationships with Network Hospitals**\nExpansion of Network of Preferred Partner Network (PPN) Hospitals\n\n2 **Auto Adjudication**\nPaperless Auto Adjudication Portal for Health Insurance Claims Processing\n\n3 **Robust Fraud Detection**\nReal Time Detection of Outliers in Claims Based on Disease, Treatment Provider, Location And Policy Seller\n\n4 **Billing Review**\nRandom Checks and Case-Specific Triggers to Identify Anomalies\n\n5 **Case Management**\nCost Component Review on a Claim-by-Claim Basis with Medical Providers\n\n---\n\n## Our Growing Hospital Network and PPN Hospitals Helps Improve Customer 5 Satisfaction Levels While Improving Control on Cost of Claims\n\n<u><strong>Rapidly Growing Network of Hospitals (#)</strong></u>\n\n| Category | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| FY2022 | 8562 |\n| FY2023 | 10005 |\n| FY2024 | 10460 |\n| 9M'FY2025 | 10299 |\n\n<u><strong>Rapidly Growing Preferred Partner Network (#)</strong></u>\n\n| Category | Series 1 (unlabelled) (#) | Preferred Partner Network Live in Cities (#) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| FY2023 | 201 | 9 |\n| FY2024 | 326 | 20 |\n| 9M'FY2025 | 455 | 35 |\n\nPreferred Partner Network Live in Cities (#)\n\n## Benefits of PPN Hospitals\n\n## For Customers\n\nFree ambulance \nservices and \ndesignated \nrelationship manager\n\nDiscount on \npharmacy, diagnostics \nand consultations \neven after discharge\n\nPPN claims \ncontribution in \nPPN cities ~14%\n\n## For Niva Bupa\n\nFavourable discount \npackages, controlling \ncost of claims\n\n---\n\n## 5 Our Domain Knowledge and Experience in Claims Cost Management\n\n## End-to-End Cashless Claims Auto Adjudication\n\n**PROVIDER CREATES CLAIMS:**\n**UPLOADS DOCUMENT**\n\n**PAYABILITY CHECK:**\n**APPROVED**\n\n**TARIFF APPLICATION:**\n**APPROVED AMOUNT**\n\n**ALL RULES CHECKED**\n**BY SYSTEM**\n\n<u><strong>Retail Health Claims Cost Index<sup>1</sup> I CAGR<sup>2</sup>- 6.6%</strong></u>\n\n| Category | Retail Health Claims Cost Index |\n| --- | --- |\n| FY2019 | 100 |\n| FY2020 | 101 |\n| FY2021 | 123 |\n| FY2022 | 128 |\n| FY2023 | 130 |\n| FY2024 | 140 |\n| 9M'FY2025 | 144 |\n\n## From ~30 mins to less than couple of minutes\n\nReduction in processing time for pre-authorization of\ncashless claims through manual processing vs auto-adjudication \nclaims system\n[Image: Image744] [Image: Image746]\n\n**Enables faster processing of retail cashless claims, reduces errors \nand promotes cost-savings**\n[Image: Image716]\n[Image: Image714]\n\nRetail Health Claim Cost Index reflects Niva Bupa YOY \naverage claim size with FY2019 as base year.\n\nThe change in index is on account of medical cost \ninflation, change in disease mix, medical 4\nadvancement etc. \n[Image: Image750]\n\n---\n\n## 6 Focus on Talent Management & Execution\n\n**2021**\n\nGreat Place To Work.\n\n**2022**\n\nGreat Place To Work.\n\nBest Workplaces\n\n**2023**\n\nGreat Place To Work.\n\nBest Workplaces\n\nGreat Place To Work.\n\nBest Workplaces\n\n**2024**\n\nBest Workplaces\n\nTHE ECONOMIC TIMES\n\nBest Workplaces in General & Health Insurance\n\n**2025**\n\nGreat Place To Work.\n\n---\n\n## Agenda\n\nOur Strategy\n\nFinancial Performance\n\n---\n\n## Financial Performance\n\n**Gross Written Premium (GWP)**\n\n| Category | Gross Written Premium (GWP) (\u20b9 in Crores) |\n| --- | --- |\n| FY2023 | 4073.0 |\n| FY2024 | 5607.6 |\n| 9M'FY2024 | 3848.1 |\n| 9M'FY2025 | 4683.6 |\n\n**Profit/(Loss) After Tax (I-GAAP)**\n\n*(\u20b9 in Crores)*\n\n| Category | Profit/(Loss) After Tax (I-GAAP) (\u20b9 in Crores) |\n| --- | --- |\n| FY2023 | 12.5 |\n| FY2024 | 81.9 |\n| 9M'FY2024 | -75.2 |\n| 9M'FY2025 | 7.4 |\n\n**Combined Ratio**\n\n| Category | Claims Ratio (%) | Expense Ratio (%) | Combined Ratio (%) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| FY2023 | 54.1 | 43.2 | 97.2 |\n| FY2024 | 59.0 | 39.8 | 98.8 |\n| 9M'FY2024 | 63.1 | 40.1 | 103.2 |\n| 9M'FY2025 | 63.4 | 41.6 | 105.0 |\n| 9M'FY2025 Without 1/n | 61.1 | 39.8 | 100.9 |\n\n**Profit/(Loss) After Tax (IFRS)**\n\n*(\u20b9 in Crores)*\n\n| Category | Profit/(Loss) After Tax (I-GAAP) (\u20b9 in Crores) | Profit/(Loss) After Tax (IFRS) (\u20b9 in Crores) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| FY2023 | 12.5 | 8.5 |\n| FY2024 | 81.9 | 106.4 |\n| 9M'FY2024 | -75.2 | 45.1 |\n| 9M'FY2025 | 7.4 | 119.5 |\n\n---\n\n**Reconciliation from I-GAAP to IFRS**\n\n| Particulars ( \u20b9 in Crores) | FY2023 | FY2024 | 9M'FY2024 | 9M'FY2025 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Profit After Taxes as per I-GAAP | 12.5 | 81.9 | (75.2) | 7.4 |\n| IFRS Adjustments |  |  |  |  |\n| Insurance Contracts [IFRS-17] | 13.8 | 68.7 | 145.8 | 168.9 |\n| Leases [IFRS-16] | (3.2) | (3.0) | (2.4) | (1.2) |\n| Financial Instruments [IFRS-09] | (1.7) | 3.5 | 0.4 | (2.3) |\n| Share-based Payment [IFRS-02] | (9.4) | (8.8) | (6.5) | (10.6) |\n| Employee Benefits [IAS-19] | - | 0.7 | 0.5 | 1.6 |\n| Income Taxes [IAS-12] | (3.5) | (36.6) | (17.5) | (44.2) |\n| Profit After Taxes as per IFRS | 8.5 | 106.4 | 45.1 | 119.5 |\n\n---\n\n## Robust Approach to Investment Management has Resulted in Strong Growth in AUM and Yield\n\n**AUM Growth**\n(\u20b9 in Crores)\n\n| Category | AUM (\u20b9 in Crores) | Investment Yield\u00b9 (%) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| FY2022 | 2401.3 | 6.6 |\n| FY2023 | 3366.1 | 6.7 |\n| FY2024 | 5458.2 | 7.1 |\n| 9M'FY2025 | 7310.7 | 7.4 |\n\n**Breakup by Ratings**\n% of Book Value of Debt Securities| 9M\u2019FY2025\n\n**Note:**\n1. Investment yield is on annualized basis for 9M\u2019FY2025\n\n| Category | Share (%) |\n| --- | --- |\n| AAA Rated | 63.6 |\n| AA / AA+ | 5.7 |\n| Sovereign | 30.7 |\n\n---\n\nAppendix\n\n---\n\n## Glossary\n\n**API** - Application Programming Interface\n\n**App** - Application\n\n**AUM** - Assets under Management\n\n**Avg** - Average\n\n**BMI** - Body Mass Index\n\n**CAGR** - Compounded Annual Growth Rate\n\n**DII** - Domestic Institutional Investor\n\n**EOM** - Expense of Management\n\n**Excl** - Excluding\n\n**FII** - Foreign Institutional Investors\n\n**FY** - Financial Year\n\n**GDPI** - Gross Direct Premium Income\n\n**GWP** - Gross Written Premium\n\n**HNI** - High Net worth Individuals\n\n**IFRS** - International Financial Reporting Standards\n\n**I-GAAP** -Indian Generally Accepted Accounting Principles\n\n**LTV** - Life Time Value\n\n**MAU** - Monthly Active Users\n\n**Mn** - Million\n\n**NBFC** - Non-Banking Financial Company\n\n**NWP** - Net Written Premium\n\n**NEP** - Net Earned Premium\n\n**NPS** - Net Promoter Score\n\n**PA** - Personal Accident\n\n**PAT** - Profit After Tax\n\n**PB** - Policy Bazaar\n\n**PBT** - Profit Before Tax\n\n**PPN** - Preferred Partner Network\n\n**RBI** - Reserve Bank of India\n\n**RI** - Reinsurance\n\n**ROAE** - Returnon Average Equity\n\n**\u20b9** - Indian Rupees\n\n---\n\n## Thank You"}}, "step10_CodeRunner6": {"step": 10, "title": "Python Execution: From the full text of the Niva Bupa Dec-31-2024 statutory financial results PDF (NL-1 Revenue Accoun...", "toolName": "CodeRunner", "snippet": "Output: Gross Premiums Written: 468,358 Lakhs -> 4,683.58 Crore\nNet Premium Written: 369,732 Lakhs -> 3,697.32 Crore\nNet Earned Premium (reported as 'Profit (Loss) in BMP' line): 307,404 Lakhs -> 3,074.04 Cro...", "raw_data": {"code": "From the full text of the Niva Bupa Dec-31-2024 statutory financial results PDF (NL-1 Revenue Account / Annexure-I and Annexure-II), extract and structure the following for the 'Year to date ended December 31, 2024' (9MFY25 cumulative) column ONLY (not the three-months column): Gross Premiums Written, Net Premium Written, Net Earned Premium (may be labeled differently e.g. 'Profit/Loss in BMP' - identify the correct NEP line), Income from Investments, Total income, Net Commission, Operating expenses, Incurred Claims (Claims Paid + Change in Outstanding Claims), Total Expense, Profit After Tax (locate PAT/Provision for tax rows further in the statement), and all analytical ratios in section 5 of Annexure-I: Solvency ratio, Claims ratio / Incurred claims ratio, Commission ratio, Expense of Management ratio, Combined ratio, Expense ratio, NPA ratios, Yield on Investments (with and without unrealized gains), and Net worth / Shareholders funds and Total Investments from the balance sheet if shown. Convert all Rs. in Lakhs figures to INR crore (divide by 100). Present a clean table: line_item | value_in_INR_crore_or_percent | as published note. Flag any line item NOT found in the document as 'NOT PUBLISHED - leave blank', do not estimate or compute derived ratios yourself.", "result": "Gross Premiums Written: 468,358 Lakhs -> 4,683.58 Crore\nNet Premium Written: 369,732 Lakhs -> 3,697.32 Crore\nNet Earned Premium (reported as 'Profit (Loss) in BMP' line): 307,404 Lakhs -> 3,074.04 Crore\nIncome from Investments (Net): 19,357 Lakhs -> 193.57 Crore\nTotal income (as reported, rows 3 to 5): 375,953 Lakhs -> 3,759.53 Crore\nNet Commission: 76,907 Lakhs -> 769.07 Crore\nOperating Expenses related to insurance business: 52,111 Lakhs -> 521.11 Crore\nClaims Paid: 206,018 Lakhs -> 2,060.18 Crore\nChange in Outstanding Claims (incl. IBNR/IBNER): 7,479 Lakhs -> 74.79 Crore\nTotal Expense (as reported): 367,442 Lakhs -> 3,674.42 Crore\nNet Profit after Tax: 744 Lakhs -> 7.44 Crore\nNet Worth / Shareholders' Funds: 286,884 Lakhs -> 2,868.84 Crore\nGross NPA (absolute, Rs.): 6,324 Lakhs -> 63.24 Crore\nNet NPA (absolute, Rs.): 0 Lakhs -> 0.0 Crore\n\nIncurred Claims (Claims Paid + Change in O/s Claims): 213,497 Lakhs -> 2,134.97 Crore\n"}}}</sources>
